<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
App Group entitlement for ThinkLessScheduleMore.

Grants this app access to the group.com.landonkea.thinklessschedulemore
shared container, which is how MessageStore hands "next scheduled send"
state to the ThinkLessScheduleMoreWidget extension (see
../Shared/NextSendSnapshot.swift for the full explanation).
ThinkLessScheduleMoreWidget.entitlements declares the SAME group string —
both targets must list an identical App Group for the shared container to
resolve to the same place for each process.

NOTE ON LOCAL/CI BUILDS WITHOUT A SIGNING TEAM: App Groups are normally
provisioned through a paid Apple Developer account. In this repo (no
committed signing team, "sign to run locally" style local builds),
UserDefaults(suiteName:) against this group may resolve to nil rather than
a real shared container. NextSendSnapshotStore treats that as "shared
state unavailable" and no-ops gracefully — the app's own scheduling is
unaffected; only the widget would show its empty state until a real
provisioning profile with this App Group capability is set up.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>group.com.landonkea.thinklessschedulemore</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
